<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scattery Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Scattery Island is a small island in the Shannon estuary off Kilrush, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-clare">County Clare</a>, Ireland. St Senan founded a monastery there in the 6th century, and its round tower and churches survive. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a> used the island as a base, and in 977 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a> attacked it and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivar-of-limerick">Ivar of Limerick</a> and his sons there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scattery-island.jpg" alt="Scattery Island" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adrian Beney · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scattery_Island_from_the_air_-_geograph.org.uk_-_594050.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
